<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWreckScatter.xml        S6 "burning-shallows wreck salvage", the scatter half
  ============================================================================
  RUT_ScaldWrecks.xml declares the three salvage buildings; this file places them.
  SALVAGE_WRECKAGE_EVERYWHERE_1 slice 3 (2026-10-06) moved it onto the shared wreck engine
  (src/RimMandrake/Wreckage, composed into mandrake.rm.biomes beside this mod): ONE weighted-list
  RM_GenStep_WreckField replaces the three GenStepDefs that GenStep_ScatterThings' single
  <thingDef> forced (RUT_Jawa_ScatterScaldWreck{Hull,Tank,Frame}, orders 965-967).

  Gate: settingsKey "Scald" is the per-biome "Wreck field: Scald" checkbox in the Wreckage
  settings, and TerminalBiomes registers the bare "Scald" gate for its biome switch, so the
  field also stops when the Scald is off. The old S6 checkbox is folded into it; gateAliases
  keeps the RM_MechanicGates key "Scald.S6" meaning this field (design §6).

  Terrain: tag-based, as before. Every cell within terrainValidationRadius 2 (a 2x2 footprint
  plus one ring) must carry RUT_ScaldShallow, which only the three shallow RUT_ScaldWater*
  terrains carry, so wrecks land only in the Scald's shallow band. allowInWaterBiome true is
  required: the Scald is a water body. The wrecks' family sets Walkable affordance.

  TUNING, ALL PROVISIONAL. The Scald shallows are the Moderate class (design §3d-i), but
  countPer10kCellsRange 1.2~1.8 overrides the class's 1.5~3 to keep the shipped ceiling (three
  steps at 0.4~0.6 each). It is a CEILING on attempts: the terrain tag rejects every cell
  outside the shallow band, so the realised count is expected well under it. minSpacing 6 now
  spaces fields of ANY wreck kind (it used to space only same-kind wrecks), and the class's
  cluster chance lets 2-3 wrecks fall together; real density is owed to a live Scald map.
  Equal weights, as the three steps had equal ranges.

  order 965: after JawaScrapfields' 960 and after terrain generation, so the RUT_ScaldWater*
  grid and its tags exist when the validator reads them.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RM_WreckField_Scald</defName>
    <label>Scald</label>
    <order>965</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.Wreckage.RM_GenStep_WreckField">
      <settingsKey>Scald</settingsKey>
      <gateAliases>
        <li>Scald.S6</li>
      </gateAliases>
      <densityClass>RM_WreckDensity_Moderate</densityClass>
      <wrecks>
        <RUT_ScaldWreckHull>1</RUT_ScaldWreckHull>
        <RUT_ScaldWreckTank>1</RUT_ScaldWreckTank>
        <RUT_ScaldWreckFrame>1</RUT_ScaldWreckFrame>
      </wrecks>
      <countPer10kCellsRange>1.2~1.8</countPer10kCellsRange>
      <allowInWaterBiome>true</allowInWaterBiome>
      <minSpacing>6</minSpacing>
      <terrainValidationRadius>2</terrainValidationRadius>
      <terrainValidationAllowed>
        <li>RUT_ScaldShallow</li>
      </terrainValidationAllowed>
    </genStep>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
